    },
    "**Language Evolution**: English changes over time. \"Suffer the little children\" (KJV) means \"let\" not \"cause pain.\"": {},
    "**Source Texts**: Translators use different ancient manuscripts. Older doesn't always mean better—scholars weigh manuscript quality, not just age.": {},
    "**Textual Discoveries**: Since 1611, thousands of earlier manuscripts have been found, improving our understanding of the original text.": {},
    "**Translation Philosophy**: Some prioritize word-for-word accuracy (formal equivalence), others thought-for-thought clarity (dynamic equivalence).": {},
